 # Recoverable dependency scheduler
 
-Implementation and self-test documentation goes here.
+`scheduler.cjs` exports `{ createScheduler }`. Create one with
+`createScheduler({ file, concurrency, execute, onStage })`, then call
+`await enqueue(jobs)`, `await run()`, and `snapshot()`.
+
+Jobs use lowercase IDs (`^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$`). `dependsOn` defaults to an
+empty array and `payload` to `null`. Batches are validated and checkpointed
+atomically; checkpoints are JSON files replaced by a same-directory temporary
+file and rename. Missing parent directories are created.
+
+`run()` claims ready jobs in ID order, up to the configured concurrency. A
+claim increments `attempt` and is durable before `execute({id, payload,
+attempt})` starts. Failed jobs and all of their descendants become blocked;
+completed jobs, including their JSON result, are never replayed. A restart
+turns durable `running` jobs back into `pending`, providing at-least-once
+recovery. This means an interrupted side effect may be performed again; use
+idempotent operations or an external idempotency key when necessary.
+
+Run the self-tests with:
+
+```text
+node --test test.cjs
+```
